{
  "note": [
    "Tile swizzle address equations for the PS5's 64 KiB render-target (R_X) and",
    "depth (Z_X) tile modes: a fixed set of XOR terms over the coordinate bits.",
    "A base term (coord, shift, mask) contributes ((coord << shift) & mask) for",
    "shift > 0, ((coord >> -shift) & mask) for shift < 0 and (coord & mask) for",
    "shift 0, with coord 1 = y, 2 = z and 3 = array slice; a column term is the",
    "same form over x. Terms are combined by exclusive or.",
    "",
    "Provenance: transcribed from SharpProspero,",
    "src/SharpProspero/Graphics/Agc/AgcTilingTables.cs (Copyright (C) 2026 SvenGDK,",
    "GPL-3.0), which records them from the graphics address library's generated",
    "equation tables -- the same library this repository builds as an oracle in",
    "tools/mip-layout-oracle.cpp. This file is that GPL-3.0 text; the check that",
    "reads it (tools/check-tile-equations.py) is this repository's own code under",
    "GPL-3.0-or-later."
  ],
